<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<model version="NetLogo 7.0.4" snapToGrid="true">
  <code><![CDATA[extensions [py]
breed [motif-nodes motif-node]
breed [cell-markers cell-marker]
directed-link-breed [regulations regulation]
motif-nodes-own [node-name activity]

globals [
  ready? busy? active-mode python-path backend-file live-parameters
  hidden-constants constants-mode
  simulation-time current-input activity-A activity-B activity-C
  baseline-C baseline-settled? settled-now? event-valid?
  recovery-error peak-response sensitivity-score precision-score recovery-time
  run-status event-finished? summary-printed? sweep-results sweep-pass-percent
  job-running? result-ready? report-pending? optimization-status job-context job-kind
]
;; Widget variables: k1 k2 k3 k4 k5 k6 initial-A initial-B initial-C
;; motif-mode ligand-level sweep-parameter search-range-factor
;; Do not duplicate widget variables in globals.


to-report default-constants [mode]
  if mode = "NFBLB" [report (list 1 1 0.000001 0.000001 0.05 0.05)]
  report (list 1 1 0.000001 10000 0.05 0.05)
end

to nfblb-defaults
  if busy? = true [stop]
  set motif-mode "NFBLB"
  set k1 1 set k2 1 set k3 0.05 set k4 0.025 set k5 10 set k6 10
  common-defaults
end

to ifflp-defaults
  if busy? = true [stop]
  set motif-mode "IFFLP"
  set k1 1 set k2 1 set k3 0.05 set k4 500 set k5 10 set k6 10
  common-defaults
end

to common-defaults
  set hidden-constants default-constants motif-mode
  set constants-mode motif-mode
  set initial-A 0.5 set initial-B 0.5 set initial-C 0.5
  set ligand-level 1.2 set search-range-factor 2 set sweep-parameter "k1"
  set ready? false
end

to-report current-parameters
  let tail default-constants motif-mode
  if (constants-mode = motif-mode) and (is-list? hidden-constants) [
    if length hidden-constants = 6 [set tail hidden-constants]
  ]
  report sentence (list k1 k2 k3 k4 k5 k6) tail
end

to-report valid-settings?
  if not member? motif-mode ["NFBLB" "IFFLP"] [user-message "Choose a motif." report false]
  if min current-parameters <= 0 [user-message "All 12 parameters must be positive." report false]
  let initial-values (list initial-A initial-B initial-C)
  if (min initial-values < 0) or (max initial-values > 1) [user-message "Initial activities must lie in [0,1]." report false]
  report true
end

to setup
  if busy? = true [stop]
  if not valid-settings? [stop]
  let captured-parameters current-parameters

  clear-all
  set hidden-constants sublist captured-parameters 6 12 set constants-mode motif-mode
  set busy? true set ready? false
  set job-running? false set result-ready? false set report-pending? false
  set optimization-status "Idle: apply a stimulus" set job-context [] set job-kind ""
  set sweep-results [] set sweep-pass-percent 0
  ;; EDIT THESE TWO PATHS IF NECESSARY.
  set python-path "D:/programmes/Anaconda/python.exe"
  set backend-file "C:/Users/prest/OneDrive/Desktop/adaptation_backend.py"
  carefully [
    if not file-exists? backend-file [error "Backend file not found; edit backend-file in setup."]
    py:setup python-path
    py:set "backend_path" backend-file
    py:run "exec(compile(open(backend_path, encoding='utf-8').read(), backend_path, 'exec'))"
    py:set "nl_mode" motif-mode py:set "nl_parameters" current-parameters
    py:set "nl_initial" (list initial-A initial-B initial-C)
    py:run "initialize(nl_mode,nl_parameters,nl_initial)"
    set active-mode motif-mode set live-parameters current-parameters set summary-printed? false
    read-state draw-view reset-ticks initialize-plots update-display clear-output
    output-print "Ready. Live k edits preserve state, time and plots."
    output-print "Optimize searches ALL 12 parameters, including Michaelis constants."
    output-print "Commands: sensitivity-analysis, save-data, save-results, inspect-data, load-parameters."
    output-print (word "Settled now? " settled-now?)
    set ready? true
  ] [user-message (word "SETUP ERROR: " error-message)]
  set busy? false
end

to reset-simulation
  setup
end

to sync-live-parameters
  if current-parameters != live-parameters [
    py:set "nl_parameters" current-parameters
    let changed? py:runresult "update_parameters(nl_parameters)"
    set live-parameters current-parameters
    if changed? [
      set result-ready? false set report-pending? false set summary-printed? true
      set optimization-status "Rates changed: settle, then stimulate"
      output-print (word "Rates changed at t=" precision simulation-time 2 "; state/time/plots preserved.")
    ]
  ]
end

to go
  if (ready? = true) and (busy? != true) [
    if motif-mode != active-mode [user-message "Topology changes require Setup." stop]
    if min current-parameters <= 0 [user-message "Use positive parameter values." stop]
    carefully [
      sync-live-parameters
      py:run "advance()"
      read-state update-display tick
      if (result-ready? = true) and (job-context != current-job-context) [
        set result-ready? false set optimization-status "Outdated result: Optimize again"
      ]
      if event-finished? and not summary-printed? [
        print-summary set summary-printed? true set report-pending? event-valid?
      ]
    ] [
      set ready? false set optimization-status (word "Simulation halted: " error-message)
      output-print optimization-status
      output-print (word "Last valid t=" simulation-time " | A B C=" (list activity-A activity-B activity-C))
      output-print (word "Parameters=" current-parameters " | input=" current-input)
      draw-status stop
    ]
    ;; Worker failures do not halt the live trajectory.
    carefully [
      if (ticks mod 10 = 0) and (job-running? = true) [check-job]
      if (report-pending? = true) and (job-running? != true) and (result-ready? != true) [
        set report-pending? false start-job "report"
      ]
    ] [
      set job-running? false set report-pending? false
      set optimization-status "Background error: see Output (live model continues)"
      output-print error-message
    ]
    draw-status
  ]
end

to apply-stimulus
  if busy? = true [stop]
  if ready? != true [user-message "Click Setup first." stop]
  if motif-mode != active-mode [user-message "Topology changes require Setup." stop]
  if not valid-settings? [stop]
  carefully [
    sync-live-parameters py:set "nl_ligand" ligand-level py:run "apply_stimulus(nl_ligand)"
    set summary-printed? false set result-ready? false set report-pending? false
    read-state update-display
    set optimization-status "New event: blue reference captured"
    output-print (word "Stimulus at t=" precision simulation-time 2 " | input=" current-input)
    if not baseline-settled? [output-print "Unsettled starting state: exploratory, not a clean adaptation test."]
    draw-status
  ] [user-message error-message]
end

to read-state
  let r py:runresult "export_state()"
  set simulation-time item 0 r set activity-A item 1 r set activity-B item 2 r
  set activity-C item 3 r set current-input item 4 r set baseline-C item 5 r
  set baseline-settled? item 6 r set recovery-error item 7 r set peak-response item 8 r
  set sensitivity-score item 9 r set precision-score item 10 r set recovery-time item 11 r
  set run-status item 12 r set event-finished? item 13 r set settled-now? item 14 r set event-valid? item 15 r
end

to-report motif-structure
  let selected motif-mode
  if ready? = true [set selected active-mode]
  if selected = "NFBLB" [report "I -> A; A -> C; C -> B; B inhibits C"]
  if selected = "IFFLP" [report "I -> A; A -> B; A -> C; B inhibits C"]
  report "Choose a motif"
end

to draw-view
  resize-world -8 8 -6 6 set-patch-size 27 ask patches [set pcolor white]
  make-node "I" -6 1 make-node "A" -2 1 make-node "B" 2 4 make-node "C" 5 1
  connect-nodes "I" "A" "+" connect-nodes "A" "C" "+"
  ifelse active-mode = "NFBLB" [connect-nodes "C" "B" "+"] [connect-nodes "A" "B" "+"]
  connect-nodes "B" "C" "INHIBITS"
  create-cell-markers 1 [setxy -5 -3 set shape "circle" set size 2 set label-color black]
  ask patch 1 -3 [set plabel "Red: C | blue: pre-stimulus baseline" set plabel-color black]
  ask patch 1 -4 [set plabel "Green: in band | red: above | blue: below | gray: invalid test" set plabel-color black]
end

to make-node [title xpos ypos]
  create-motif-nodes 1 [set node-name title setxy xpos ypos set shape "circle" set size 1.6 set label-color black]
end

to connect-nodes [source-name target-name edge-label]
  let source-node one-of motif-nodes with [node-name = source-name]
  let target-node one-of motif-nodes with [node-name = target-name]
  ask source-node [create-regulation-to target-node [
    set label edge-label set label-color black set thickness 0.15
    ifelse edge-label = "INHIBITS" [set color red] [set color gray]
  ]]
end

to initialize-plots
  set-current-plot "Input stimulus" set-plot-x-range 0 1000 set-plot-y-range 0 2
  create-temporary-plot-pen "Applied input" set-plot-pen-color black
  set-current-plot "Output and recovery band" set-plot-x-range 0 1000 set-plot-y-range 0 1
  foreach ["C" "Baseline" "Upper 2%" "Lower 2%"] [p -> create-temporary-plot-pen p]
  set-current-plot-pen "C" set-plot-pen-color red
  set-current-plot-pen "Baseline" set-plot-pen-color blue
  set-current-plot-pen "Upper 2%" set-plot-pen-color gray
  set-current-plot-pen "Lower 2%" set-plot-pen-color gray
  set-current-plot "Internal activities" set-plot-x-range 0 1000 set-plot-y-range 0 1
  foreach ["A" "B" "C"] [p -> create-temporary-plot-pen p]
  set-current-plot-pen "A" set-plot-pen-color blue
  set-current-plot-pen "B" set-plot-pen-color green
  set-current-plot-pen "C" set-plot-pen-color red
  set-current-plot "Batch responses" set-plot-x-range 0 300 set-plot-y-range 0 2
end

to update-display
  ask motif-nodes [
    if node-name = "I" [set activity current-input]
    if node-name = "A" [set activity activity-A]
    if node-name = "B" [set activity activity-B]
    if node-name = "C" [set activity activity-C]
    set label (word node-name " = " precision activity 3)
    ifelse node-name = "I" [set color gray] [set color scale-color blue activity 0 1]
  ]
  ask cell-markers [
    ifelse (not baseline-settled?) or (not event-valid?) [set color gray set label "Exploratory / interrupted"] [
      let deviation (activity-C - baseline-C) / baseline-C
      ifelse abs deviation <= .02 [set color green set label "Within band"] [
        ifelse deviation > 0 [set color red set label "Above baseline"] [set color blue set label "Below baseline"]
      ]
    ]
  ]
  set-current-plot "Input stimulus" set-current-plot-pen "Applied input" plotxy simulation-time current-input
  set-current-plot "Output and recovery band"
  set-current-plot-pen "C" plotxy simulation-time activity-C
  set-current-plot-pen "Baseline" plotxy simulation-time baseline-C
  set-current-plot-pen "Upper 2%" plotxy simulation-time (baseline-C * 1.02)
  set-current-plot-pen "Lower 2%" plotxy simulation-time (baseline-C * .98)
  set-current-plot "Internal activities"
  set-current-plot-pen "A" plotxy simulation-time activity-A
  set-current-plot-pen "B" plotxy simulation-time activity-B
  set-current-plot-pen "C" plotxy simulation-time activity-C
end

to print-summary
  output-print "===== LIVE EVENT: first 300 time units ====="
  output-print (word "Error=" precision recovery-error 5 "% | peak=" precision peak-response 3 "%")
  output-print (word "Ligand S=" precision sensitivity-score 4 " | P=" precision precision-score 3
    " | recovery=" precision recovery-time 2)
  output-print run-status
  output-print "Robustness is a separate equilibrated-configuration test."
end

to optimize
  request-job "optimize"
end

to sensitivity-analysis
  request-job "sensitivity"
end

to robustness-report
  request-job "report"
end

to request-job [kind]
  if busy? = true [stop]
  if ready? != true [user-message "Click Setup first." stop]
  if motif-mode != active-mode [user-message "Topology changes require Setup." stop]
  if not valid-settings? [stop]
  carefully [
    sync-live-parameters
    if (job-running? = true) and ((job-kind = "report") or (job-context != current-job-context)) [
      py:run "stop_job()" set job-running? false set report-pending? false
    ]
    if job-running? = true [
      check-job
      if job-running? = true [user-message (word "Background: " optimization-status) stop]
    ]
    if (kind = "optimize") and (result-ready? = true) and (job-context = current-job-context) [apply-ready stop]
    set result-ready? false set report-pending? false
    start-job kind
  ] [set optimization-status "Background start error: see Output" output-print error-message]
  draw-status
end

to-report current-job-context
  report (list active-mode current-parameters ligand-level search-range-factor current-input)
end

to start-job [kind]
  set job-kind kind
  ifelse kind = "report" [py:set "selected_ligand" current-input] [py:set "selected_ligand" ligand-level]
  py:set "requested_kind" kind py:set "requested_factor" search-range-factor
  let info py:runresult "prepare_job(requested_kind,selected_ligand,requested_factor)"
  let bank []
  if kind = "optimize" [
    let index 0
    repeat (item 0 info) [
      py:set "candidate_index" index
      let row py:runresult "get_candidate(candidate_index)"
      set bank lput (fit-to-controls (item 1 row)) bank
      set index index + 1
    ]
  ]
  py:set "fitted_bank" bank py:set "configured_backend" backend-file py:set "configured_python" python-path
  let folder py:runresult "launch_job(configured_backend,configured_python,fitted_bank)"
  set job-context current-job-context set job-running? true set result-ready? false
  set optimization-status (word "Background " kind " | " item 1 info " -> " item 2 info)
  output-print optimization-status output-print (word "Worker files/log: " folder)
end

to check-job
  let result py:runresult "poll_job()"
  let kind item 0 result
  if kind = "running" [set optimization-status item 1 result stop]
  if kind = "idle" [set job-running? false stop]
  set job-running? false
  if (kind = "stale") or (job-context != current-job-context) [
    set result-ready? false set optimization-status "Outdated snapshot: not applied" output-print optimization-status stop
  ]
  if kind = "error" [set result-ready? false set optimization-status "Background error: see Output" output-print item 1 result stop]
  if kind = "report" [
    set optimization-status (word "Qnear=" item 1 result "/" item 3 result " | Qwide=" item 2 result "/" item 3 result)
    output-print "===== LOCAL ROBUSTNESS REPORT =====" output-print optimization-status
    output-print (word "Nominal passes? " item 4 result " | " item 5 result " | numerical failures=" item 6 result)
    output-print "Each trial uses its own pre-stimulus baseline. Finite samples, not paper-global Q."
  ]
  if kind = "sensitivity" [
    set optimization-status "Sensitivity complete: see Output or save-results"
    print-sensitivity
  ]
  if kind = "optimized" [
    output-print "===== ALL-12-PARAMETER VALIDATION =====" output-print item 8 result
    if item 7 result > 0 [
      output-print (word "Nearby: original " item 3 result "/" item 7 result " | candidate " item 4 result "/" item 7 result)
      output-print (word "Wider: original " item 5 result "/" item 7 result " | candidate " item 6 result "/" item 7 result)
      output-print (word "Numerical failures: original=" item 9 result " | candidate=" item 10 result)
    ]
    set result-ready? item 1 result
    ifelse result-ready? [set optimization-status "READY TO APPLY: click Optimize again"]
      [set optimization-status "No validated improvement; existing values kept"]
    output-print optimization-status print-sensitivity plot-optimization
  ]
end

to print-sensitivity
  output-print "Parameter sensitivity (not ligand S): name | max normalized effect | time | tail effect"
  let rows py:runresult "sensitivity_summary()"
  foreach rows [row -> output-print (word item 0 row " | valid? " item 1 row
    " | max=" item 2 row " | t=" item 3 row " | tail=" item 4 row)]
end

to apply-ready
  let previous current-parameters
  set busy? true
  carefully [
    let values py:runresult "ready_values()"
    if length values != 12 [error "No current 12-parameter suggestion."]
    if (fit-to-controls values) != values [error "Controls cannot represent the suggested k values."]
    py:run "apply_result()"
    set-all-controls values
    set live-parameters current-parameters
    set result-ready? false set report-pending? false set summary-printed? true
    read-state update-display
    set optimization-status "APPLIED all 12 without reset; settle then stimulate"
    output-print optimization-status show-parameters
  ] [set-all-controls previous set result-ready? false set optimization-status "Apply error: see Output" output-print error-message]
  set busy? false draw-status
end

to set-all-controls [values]
  set k1 item 0 values set k2 item 1 values set k3 item 2 values
  set k4 item 3 values set k5 item 4 values set k6 item 5 values
  set hidden-constants sublist values 6 12 set constants-mode motif-mode
end

to-report fit-to-controls [proposed]
  let previous current-parameters
  let fitted proposed let issue ""
  carefully [set-all-controls proposed set fitted current-parameters] [set issue error-message]
  set-all-controls previous
  if issue != "" [error issue]
  if min fitted <= 0 [error "Give k sliders positive minima."]
  report fitted
end

to show-parameters
  (foreach ["k1" "k2" "k3" "k4" "k5" "k6" "KIA" "KFA" "KB" "KFB" "KAC" "KBC"] current-parameters
    [[name value] -> output-print (word name " = " value)])
end

to draw-status
  let shade blue
  if job-running? = true [set shade cyan]
  if result-ready? = true [set shade orange]
  if is-string? optimization-status [
    if position "APPLIED" optimization-status != false [set shade green]
    if position "error" optimization-status != false [set shade red]
    if position "halted" optimization-status != false [set shade red]
    if position "Outdated" optimization-status != false [set shade gray]
    ask patch 1 -5 [set plabel optimization-status set plabel-color shade]
  ]
end

to plot-optimization
  let data py:runresult "result_plot()"
  let times item 0 data let curves item 1 data
  set-current-plot "Batch responses" clear-plot set-plot-x-range 0 300
  let lo .9 let hi 1.1
  foreach curves [row -> set lo min (list lo min (item 1 row)) set hi max (list hi max (item 1 row))]
  let margin max (list .05 ((hi - lo) * .1))
  set-plot-y-range (max (list 0 (lo - margin))) (hi + margin)
  foreach [1 1.02 .98] [v -> create-temporary-plot-pen (word "Reference " v)
    ifelse v = 1 [set-plot-pen-color blue] [set-plot-pen-color gray] plotxy 0 v plotxy 300 v]
  let colors (list red orange violet cyan magenta brown) let index 0
  foreach curves [row -> create-temporary-plot-pen item 0 row
    set-plot-pen-color item (index mod length colors) colors
    (foreach times (item 1 row) [[t y] -> plotxy t y]) set index index + 1]
end

to save-results
  let destination user-new-file
  if destination = false [stop]
  carefully [py:set "save_path" destination py:run "save_results(save_path)"
    output-print "Saved result JSON and applicable sensitivity/candidate CSV files."] [user-message error-message]
end

to save-data
  let destination user-new-file
  if destination = false [stop]
  carefully [py:set "save_path" destination py:run "save_live_data(save_path)"
    output-print "Saved live JSON, event log and companion trajectory CSV (up to 100000 latest points)."] [user-message error-message]
end

to inspect-data
  let source user-file
  if source = false [stop]
  carefully [py:set "read_path" source
    let rows py:runresult "read_saved(read_path)"
    foreach rows [row -> output-print (word item 0 row ": " item 1 row)]] [user-message error-message]
end

to load-parameters
  if ready? != true [user-message "Setup first, with the same motif as the saved file." stop]
  let source user-file
  if source = false [stop]
  let previous current-parameters
  carefully [
    py:set "read_path" source
    let saved py:runresult "saved_parameters(read_path)"
    if item 0 saved != active-mode [error "Saved motif differs. Select that motif and Setup first."]
    let values item 1 saved
    let fitted fit-to-controls values
    if fitted != values [error "Adjust k-slider ranges/increments to represent saved values exactly."]
    py:set "loaded_values" values py:run "update_parameters(loaded_values)"
    set-all-controls values set live-parameters current-parameters
    set result-ready? false set report-pending? false set summary-printed? true
    read-state update-display
    set optimization-status "Loaded parameters, not revalidated for current event"
    output-print optimization-status
  ] [set-all-controls previous user-message error-message]
end

to export-optimization
  save-results
end

to export-sweep
  save-results
end

to export-robustness
  save-results
end

to run-batch
  optimize
end

to find-better-parameters
  optimize
end

to load-recommendation
  optimize
end
]]></code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="529" wrappingAllowedX="true" y="20" frameRate="30.0" minPycor="-6" height="354" showTickCounter="true" patchSize="27.0" fontSize="10" wrappingAllowedY="true" width="462" tickCounterLabel="ticks" maxPycor="6" updateMode="0" maxPxcor="8" minPxcor="-8"></view>
    <button x="225" y="85" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="110" display="IFFLP defaults">ifflp-defaults</button>
    <button x="235" y="360" height="60" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="235" display="apply-stimulus">apply-stimulus</button>
    <output x="990" y="360" height="275" fontSize="12" width="445"></output>
    <slider x="1450" step="0.1" y="300" max="20" width="250" display="k5" height="50" min="0.1" direction="Horizontal" default="14.9" variable="k5"></slider>
    <slider x="1450" step="0.005" y="230" max="1000" width="250" display="k4" height="50" min="0.005" direction="Horizontal" default="693.695" variable="k4"></slider>
    <slider x="1455" step="0.1" y="365" max="20" width="250" display="k6" height="50" min="0.1" direction="Horizontal" default="5.9" variable="k6"></slider>
    <slider x="1450" step="0.05" y="165" max="3" width="250" display="k3" height="50" min="0.01" direction="Horizontal" default="1.2" variable="k3"></slider>
    <slider x="1450" step="0.05" y="100" max="3" width="250" display="k2" height="50" min="0.1" direction="Horizontal" default="0.35" variable="k2"></slider>
    <slider x="1450" step="0.005" y="35" max="3" width="250" display="k1" height="50" min="0.1" direction="Horizontal" default="0.3223684210526316" variable="k1"></slider>
    <slider x="245" step="0.05" y="425" max="2" width="220" display="ligand-level" height="50" min="0.1" direction="Horizontal" default="1.3" variable="ligand-level"></slider>
    <chooser x="235" y="15" height="60" variable="motif-mode" current="1" width="250" display="motif-mode">
      <choice type="string" value="NFBLB"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="IFFLP"></choice>
    </chooser>
    <input x="230" multiline="false" y="280" height="60" variable="initial-C" type="number" width="250">0.5</input>
    <input x="230" multiline="false" y="215" height="60" variable="initial-B" type="number" width="250">0.5</input>
    <input x="230" multiline="false" y="150" height="60" variable="initial-A" type="number" width="250">0.5</input>
    <note x="0" y="595" backgroundDark="-5987164" fontSize="12" width="310" markdown="true" height="2535" textColorDark="-1" textColorLight="-16777216" backgroundLight="0"><![CDATA[# Biochemical Adaptation: NFBLB & IFFLP

## Goal
Can the output C respond to a stimulus, then return near its original level while the stimulus remains elevated?

The model compares two three-node circuits:

- NFBLB: I → A → C → B, with B inhibiting C.
- IFFLP: I → A → C and A → B, with B inhibiting C.

I = external input. A, B, C = internal active fractions.

## How to run
1. Click Load NFBLB preset or Load IFFLP preset.
2. Click Setup / Reset.
3. Click Go / Pause.
4. Select a ligand level, then click Apply stimulus.
5. Allow the output to respond and recover.

Example: changing input from 1 to 1.2 is a 20% increase.

## Presets

Both presets use:
k1 = k2 = 1
k5 = k6 = 10
Initial A = B = C = 0.5

NFBLB:
k3 = 0.05, k4 = 0.025
B is activated by C.
Under saturation: dB/dt ≈ k3·C − k4.
Therefore, the approximate target is:
C* ≈ k4/k3 = 0.5.

IFFLP:
k3 = 0.05, k4 = 500
B is activated by A.
With KFB = 10000:
dB/dt ≈ k3·A − (k4/KFB)·B.
Therefore, B* ≈ A*, allowing the opposing pathways to balance near C = 0.5.

The presets also load different hidden saturation parameters. They are illustrative—not fitted biological values.

## Reading the plots
- Input stimulus: the input actually applied.
- Output and recovery band: C, its baseline, and the ±2% recovery band.
- Internal activities: A, B, and C.
- Batch results: recovery errors across parameter tests.

Cell color:
Green = within the recovery band.
Red = above it.
Blue = below it.
Gray = unsettled starting baseline.

## Adaptation measurements

Recovery error (%) =
100 × max|C − baseline| / baseline
over the final 20 time units.

Sensitivity S =
relative peak output change / relative input change.

A successful run must respond noticeably AND recover:
S > 1, precision P > 10, recovery error ≤ 2%,
plus settled-baseline and stability checks.

Color alone does not establish adaptation.

## Run batch
Runs 42 independent simulations:
- 2 reference tests.
- 40 perturbed tests: 20 parameter sets × 2 input changes.

All 12 kinetic parameters receive random multipliers from 0.8 to 1.25.

Robustness (%) =
100 × successful perturbed tests / 40.

Green bars pass all criteria.
Red bars fail at least one—see the Output area.

A higher pass percentage means better robustness over this tested range, not a universal guarantee.

## Important
- Run batch reads the current sliders.
- The live simulation reads parameters during Setup.
- Initial values apply before equilibration.
- Moving the ligand slider does not apply it until Apply stimulus is clicked.
- For clean comparisons, use one stimulus per run.
- Setup / Reset clears the previous results.]]></note>
